 anford.edu/event/special-seminar-and-fireside-chat-understanding-work-usin
 g-ai/\n\nThe government has maintained crucial data infrastructure that al
 low jobseekers to find jobs\, employers to hire\, and researchers to predi
 ct the future of work. This infrastructure is tested by rapid changes brou
 ght about by AI\, and at the same time\, is empowered by the use of AI.\n\
 nPhil Lewis from the National Center for O*NET Development will talk about
  data infrastructure the US Department of Labor provides and how AI is use
 d to update it. A panel with Diyi Yang from the Stanford Computer Science 
 Department and DEL’s Erik Brynjolfsson will discuss the opportunities of
  a new partnership between Stanford and the National Center for O*NET Deve
 lopment.
